263}] :question/id #uuid "a302c934-1e7e-57a4-882d-8cd125952f61" :question/math-academy-id "q-48064" :question/problem "![](images/02/0218a1e13a0504b20e802100f9e15877beeb2b565a49fe7cd01cf2a0cf0197ee.png)\n\nThe graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x = 2$\n- **II.** $lim_(x → 2)f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x = 2$" :question/worked-solution "The filled point at x=2 gives f(2)=1. The left and right limits are 1 and -2, so the two-sided limit does not exist and the function is not continuous there."}]}
